        "id": "ch1_5_1-1",
        "text": "Methods\nMethod names should use lowercase. The name should consist of a single word or more\nthan one word separated by underscores. You can see an example of this here:\ncalculate_sum\nTo make the code readable, the method should preferably be a verb, related to the\nprocessing that the method is supposed to perform.\nIf a method is non-public, it should have a leading underscore. Here's an example of this:\n_my_calculate_sum\nDunder or magic methods are methods that have a leading and trailing underscore.\nExamples of Dunder or magic methods are shown here:\n\u2022 __init__\n\u2022 __add__\nIt is never a good idea to use two leading and trailing underscores to name a method,\nand the use of these by developers is discouraged. Such a naming scheme is designed for\nPython methods.",
